{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1217879-a-little-help-in-making-a-freehold","id":1217879,"title":"A little help in Making a Freehold","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-11T20:53:38-07:00","id":1217879,"title":"A little help in Making a Freehold","content":"Yes this time it will be for a real game.<br /> Here is the setting info. <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Setting Notes-</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wisconsin, it\u2019s a werewolf\u2019s paradise. Spirits and deep forests, for the hunt, cities for the human element. All other supernaturals exist here because they allow it\u2026 or they are too proud to realize that they are already there until they become too much effort to root out. Such is the case with Changelings.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changeling courts developed undetected until the huntsmen first screwed up and attacked an uratha by mistake. Courts were quickly approached and made compliant. Many packs have a Changeling ally or member, and the courts have 2 Ambassadors of the local pack in presence. These have been a rather unexpected and nasty surprise for huntsmen who thought they had passed all the defenses and were into the vulnerable heart of a court.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Changelings, the players live under the rule of the wolves. The benevolent canine overlords remind the lost who rules these lands by forcing the changelings to act in their hunts, and their monarchs swear oaths of fealty to the wolves.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Makers of Greatness</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Freehold History</span></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The maker's first found themselves in Waukesha in the early 1900\u2019s, and the Bacchanal Court was established based on the brewery industry. The court\u2019s defenses and approached are all based upon the history and story of American Beer. When the courts based around the dairy industry collapsed from the displeasure of their wolf masters their members were absorbed into the Bacchanal court which came to represent both food and drink. Later in 1941 when Les Paul invented the Electric Guitar the Changelings were there, and formed a pact to the invention, and the music that flowed forth as the Court of the Silver Strings. In 1959 when Generac was Founded the Galvanic court was too, capitalizing on the generator maker, locking their fate with Jorgensen\u2019s company. Lastly in 1974 when two 36 year old men published a game of organized make believe and weaving a story the Illusory court was born.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bacchanal Court</span></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Court Emotion: Jolly</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>\u200bI </i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>feel that the jolly drunk is what this court is going for. After the aborbed the dairy industry and gained Wisconsin's food stuff like Cheese curds (both fried and served as </i><i>squeeky cheese)</i><i>, Cheese, beer cheese, </i></span></span><i> Butter Burgers, Frozen Custard (like ice cream only 100x better and with less sugar!), and well all that wonderful fattening stuff, people who partake in the delights that the court is built around and contracted with aren't exactly going to be mean. It's hard to feel mean when your eating good food, and drinking with friends. Idealy I see this courts contracts causing effects that </i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>simulate</i></span></span><i> drunken stupor, food coma, produce food and drink or enhance it.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Silver String Court</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Court Emotion: Disappointment</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>I bet a lot of you are wondering why a court tied to the awesomeness that is the electric guitar has such an UNMETAL emotion. Disappointment? Why is that? Simple. Go look up Les Paul on Wikipedia. Even though he was first to the patent, he was last to market. For that reason he was over looked for years as an inventor. Tieing the horse to his wagon was not a bad choice because it is an interesting story, but it is not an uplifting one.</i><br /> For contracts I'm thinking effects that revolve around sound and deafse, disorientation, and depression<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Galvanic Court</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Court Emotion: Triumph</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>\u200bUnlike Les Paul, the </i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>story of </i><i>Wisconsin</i><i> and Generators goes the other direction. Who doesn't feel Triumphant when you beat back the darkness of power outage with your amazing tools. Candles are fine but when your neighbors are living by the light of candles and your lights are still on because your generator is out </i><i>there</i><i> purring away producing power for your family, you have running water, hot water, AC/Heat, and everything that makes modern life modern. </i><i>You</i><i> feel TRIUMPH. Forces of Nature, or Stupidity can't take you down and you know it. That's how I see this court. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> Contract wise, Hold on to your butts. Fixing engines. And calling down big killowatts on their heads.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Illusory Court</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Court Emotion: Wonder</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>\u200bNot quite sure what I want for Contracts here. They should </i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>have to do with illusion and imagination.</i><br /> <br /> <i>What I could do with is a look over these and some help </i><i>writing</i><i> these figuring out what more I need to do so nudges </i></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key"